  },
  {
    "script": "As soon as we sat, one of my friends, Steve, launches for the menu. And I was like, Steve, Steve, it's cool, man. I'll just order for everyone at the table. And he's like, oh, oh, that's fine, Trevor. I'll just, I'll order for myself, thank you. I was like, no, no, it's not about that, Steve. I just prefer to order for all of us, yeah?",
    "start-time": 229.60000610351562,
    "end-time": 247.89999389648438
  },
  {
    "script": "He's like, uh, I don't know why that's necessary. I think I'll just order for myself. Is that okay? I was like, uh, it's not, no, it's not okay, Steve. It's not okay, right? Because you're probably gonna say some shit that's gonna embarrass me in front of my Indian people, right? And so I just need you to back off for a moment.",
    "start-time": 252.22000122070312,
    "end-time": 267.1199951171875
  },
  {
    "script": "Every time I take my white friends to an ethnic restaurant, they always say some shit that embarrasses me. Every single time, every time. Either they don't know how to pronounce the food or they'll say some random shit. They'll be like, can I get that one, the papadums? What do you call these ones? You know, they'll be like, can I get this one, but not spicy? Kill yourself! How are you gonna ask for curry, but not spicy?",
    "start-time": 299.4200134277344,
    "end-time": 320.7799987792969
  },
  {
    "script": "The guy was Indian, his beard was Indian, but his mouth was Shrek. I didn't expect that. And now he didn't understand me because I trudeaued too much. I didn't need to try so hard. But then I realized I also couldn't stop because that would be racist. So now I've got the Scottish Indian man looking at me. Everyone's quiet and he's like, if you don't mind, laddie, could you order again a little slower this time, right?",
    "start-time": 500.2799987792969,
    "end-time": 539.5999755859375
  },
  {
    "script": "I'm like, no, you can't offend anybody. There are no mistakes here, okay? We are all friends, okay? If anybody make a mistake, we forget about it. In fact, whatever happens today, we're all going to forget about it, okay? Just order, just order. He's like, no, I wish I could. I really wish I could. But Trevor, please go.",
    "start-time": 596.739990234375,
    "end-time": 611.0399780273438
  },
  {
    "script": "The waiter was like, hey, hey, hey, hey, there's no need to fight amongst yourselves. Look, clearly your friend's a little uncomfortable, right? Just order for him. Like, yes, he's totally uncomfortable. Okay, could we please have three Romali rotis and three garlic naan, one shahi paneer, one palak paneer, and could we also get a lamb Rogan Josh, and we're also going to be having one butter chicken.",
    "start-time": 625.2000122070312,
    "end-time": 657.1400146484375
  },
  {
    "script": "For your Caucasian friends! For anybody, for anybody. Anybody can enjoy different types of curry. They don't all have to be spicy. It doesn't matter, as long as you participate. There is no wrong way. Oh, you're so understanding, Trevor. Yes, yes, I am. Could we also please get the zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz, zzz.",
    "start-time": 661.8400268554688,
    "end-time": 679.7999877929688
  },
  {
    "script": "And the waiter walks over. This beautiful Indian man. He's got his beautiful Indian garb, and he steps up. And I know, Steve, I can see him questioning my authority out of the corner of my eye. I wanted to show him that these were my people. And as the waiter got there, I didn't even let him speak. I just jumped up and I was like, good evening.",
    "start-time": 369.0799865722656,
    "end-time": 385.9200134277344
  },
  {
    "script": "I'm going to be ordering for the entire table, please. Could we please have three garlic roll naans? We're going to have three Romali rotis. Give us one shahi paneer, one palak paneer. You know what? We're going to have a Rogan Josh lamb, of course. Could we also please have one butter chicken for my Caucasian friends?",
    "start-time": 385.9200134277344,
    "end-time": 412.2799987792969
  },
  {
    "script": "And then we're going to have three samosas and three mango lassies to wash it all down. Thank you very much. I crushed it. I could feel it. Everyone could feel it. They could feel something. Because the table went dead. The waiter just stared at me. At first I thought he was impressed.",
    "start-time": 412.2799987792969,
    "end-time": 444.8599853515625
  },
  {
    "script": "Then I realized he was confused. And this Indian man leans in. And looks me dead in the eye and he's like, sorry, sir, could you repeat what you said? I kind of hear what you were saying, right? You got a bit of an accent. And I was like, oh shit! And he's like, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no. He's Scottish!",
    "start-time": 454.0799865722656,
    "end-time": 484.6400146484375
  },
  {
    "script": "I didn't expect that, right? Because the whole place is Indian. There's an Indian restaurant, the people eating, we're Indian, there's Indian gods on the wall. The guy was Indian, his beard was Indian, but his mouth was Shrek. I didn't expect that. And now he didn't understand me because I trudeaued too much. I didn't need to try so hard.",
    "start-time": 493.0400085449219,
    "end-time": 505.79998779296875
  },
  {
    "script": "So now I've got the Scottish Indian man looking at me. Everyone's quiet and he's like, if you don't mind, laddie, could you order again a little slower this time, right? And then I hear, what, yourself? You want me to place the entire order again? Ah, if you don't mind, I'm ready whenever you are. You know, I think everybody can order for themselves at the table.",
    "start-time": 539.5999755859375,
    "end-time": 570.52001953125
  },
  {
    "script": "I don't think it's necessary for me to hold their hands. Everybody can order individually and we can go from there, okay? We can go from there. And Steve was like, oh, I wish I could, but I'm so afraid I might offend someone. I think my friend here should order for us. Please, Trevor, go ahead. Go ahead. You're far more cultured than I am.",
    "start-time": 570.52001953125,
    "end-time": 583.7000122070312
  },
  {
    "script": "I said, no, no, no, no. Steve, please, you can dry your hand. I'm sure you know exactly what you want. He's like, no, but what if I say something embarrassing? The last thing I'd want to do is offend another person's culture, Trevor. Said, no, you can't offend anybody. There are no mistakes here, okay? We are all friends, okay?",
    "start-time": 585.739990234375,
    "end-time": 601.9199829101562
  },
  {
    "script": "If anybody make a mistake, we forget about it. In fact, whatever happens today, we're all going to forget about it, okay? Just order, just order. He's like, no, I wish I could. I really wish I could. But Trevor, please go. I said, no, no, you just order, Steve. He's like, oh, please, Trevor. I was like, order, bastard! Just order!",
