script_details_var:  [{'script': "Schadenfreude, German word, schadenfreude, right? It means to take great joy in the pain and suffering of others. Fun fact, that word was never translated into another language. I wonder why. My story happened in Edinburgh, Scotland. What I do whenever I'm traveling is, if I get to be in the same place as my friends, we try and spend as much time together and what we'll do is we'll order food or we'll go out and when we do that, we allow one person to designate the meal.", 'start-time': 0.0, 'end-time': 39.619998931884766}, {'script': "Whenever my day comes around, consistently, I pick Indian food, all right? Yeah, I think it's the best cuisine in the world, nothing comes close, you don't agree with me, let's meet in the parking lot, we can fight. I love Indian food, loved it my whole life. So we're in Edinburgh, I'm with my friends, they're like, where are we going? Trevor, what do you say? I'm like, Indian food. They're like, every time? I was like, yes, every time, Indian food.", 'start-time': 41.7400016784668, 'end-time': 63.439998626708984}, {'script': "And I searched, I searched for where we were gonna go because I always try and find the most authentic Indian restaurant I can find. Like, I mean like authentic Indian restaurants. Do you know what I mean? So what I'll do is I'll go to a place and then I'll ask around and I'll ask people. I'll be like, where do you go? And then like, where the white people tell me, I don't go there.", 'start-time': 68.95999908447266, 'end-time': 85.87999725341797}, {'script': 'Now, the reason it had to be so authentic, just so you understand a little bit of me. I grew up in South Africa, as you know, right? Now, what a lot of people may not know is that South Africa has one of the largest Indian populations outside of India. And so I was lucky enough to grow up surrounded by Indian culture. In fact, one of my best friends growing up was a little Indian boy by the name of Thiessen Pillay.', 'start-time': 91.68000030517578, 'end-time': 112.63999938964844}, {'script': "Thiessen would get a packed lunch from his mom every single day. Every single day, the meal was curry. I know this because every day, we'd sit down together. Thiessen would open his little lunchbox. He'd open the bread, look inside, and then he'd scream at the top of his lungs. He'd be like, curry! Damn it, mommy. I was like, oh, but Thiessen, is it bad? I don't even know anymore.", 'start-time': 114.45999908447266, 'end-time': 146.66000366210938}, {'script': "I put that sandwich in my mouth. I bit down, and my mouth came alive. My tongue discovered its purpose. I didn't know potatoes could pop like that. The flavors were bouncing around. My eyes opened wide. It was, I just, I was like, wow, I was like, curry! Thank you, mommy. It was perfect. And since then, I've loved curry.", 'start-time': 176.36000061035156, 'end-time': 207.39999389648438}, {'script': "So, fast forward many decades. We're in Edinburgh, Scotland. Going out with my friends. We're choosing a spot. I choose Indian, authentic Indian. We get to the place, and it's legit. Like, it is legit. We walk in, and there's Indian music playing. There are Indian people eating. Indian cooks in the back, Indian waiters, Indian guards on the wall. I'm like, this is it. I'm home.", 'start-time': 209.8800048828125, 'end-time': 228.0800018310547}, {'script': "As soon as we sat, one of my friends, Steve, launches for the menu. And I was like, Steve, Steve, it's cool, man. I'll just order for everyone at the table. And he's like, oh, oh, that's fine, Trevor. I'll just, I'll order for myself, thank you. I was like, no, no, it's not about that, Steve. I just prefer to order for all of us, yeah?", 'start-time': 229.60000610351562, 'end-time': 247.89999389648438}, {'script': "He's like, uh, I don't know why that's necessary. I think I'll just order for myself. Is that okay? I was like, uh, it's not, no, it's not okay, Steve. It's not okay, right? Because you're probably gonna say some shit that's gonna embarrass me in front of my Indian people, right? And so I just need you to back off for a moment.", 'start-time': 252.22000122070312, 'end-time': 267.1199951171875}, {'script': "Every time I take my white friends to an ethnic restaurant, they always say some shit that embarrasses me. Every single time, every time. Either they don't know how to pronounce the food or they'll say some random shit. They'll be like, can I get that one, the papadums? What do you call these ones? You know, they'll be like, can I get this one, but not spicy? Kill yourself! How are you gonna ask for curry, but not spicy?", 'start-time': 299.4200134277344, 'end-time': 320.7799987792969}, {'script': "The guy was Indian, his beard was Indian, but his mouth was Shrek. I didn't expect that. And now he didn't understand me because I trudeaued too much. I didn't need to try so hard. But then I realized I also couldn't stop because that would be racist. So now I've got the Scottish Indian man looking at me. Everyone's quiet and he's like, if you don't mind, laddie, could you order again a little slower this time, right?", 'start-time': 500.2799987792969, 'end-time': 539.5999755859375}, {'script': "I'm like, no, you can't offend anybody. There are no mistakes here, okay? We are all friends, okay? If anybody make a mistake, we forget about it. In fact, whatever happens today, we're all going to forget about it, okay? Just order, just order. He's like, no, I wish I could. I really wish I could. But Trevor, please go.", 'start-time': 596.739990234375, 'end-time': 611.0399780273438}, {'script': "The waiter was like, hey, hey, hey, hey, there's no need to fight amongst yourselves. Look, clearly your friend's a little uncomfortable, right? Just order for him. Like, yes, he's totally uncomfortable. Okay, could we please have three Romali rotis and three garlic naan, one shahi paneer, one palak paneer, and could we also get a lamb Rogan Josh, and we're als